.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-webhooks - Every account's webhook subscriptions, with circuit and last attempt (lists when run bare)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin webhooks [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the webhook subscriptions of every account: each with the account that owns it,
whether it is active, its circuit state and failure count, and when and how its newest
delivery attempt went. The open circuits come first.

.PP
A circuit opens after 10 consecutive failed events and never closes by itself: nothing is
delivered to that subscription until it is reset, by its merchant ('rail0 webhooks
reset-circuit') or here ('rail0 admin webhooks reset-circuit'). --circuit open lists the
subscriptions that are receiving nothing right now.

.PP
No signing key is shown: a shared secret is returned once, to the subscription's owner.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--account\fP=""
	Only this account's subscriptions (account id)

.PP
\fB--circuit\fP=""
	Only subscriptions whose circuit is open or closed

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for webhooks

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort by created_at, updated_at, circuit_failure_count or name (prefix - for descending; default: open circuits first)

.PP
\fB--topic\fP=""
	Only subscriptions that include this topic


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin webhooks --circuit open               # who is receiving nothing
  rail0 admin webhooks --account 019e748b-… --pretty
  rail0 admin webhooks --topic payments.captured --sort -circuit_failure_count
  rail0 admin deliveries --webhook 01a0f3c2-… --status failed   # what it was failing on
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin(1)\fP, \fBrail0-admin-webhooks-reset-circuit(1)\fP
